+ * controller on spi@111D0000, Google Tensor G3 ("zuma", Pixel 8 Pro).
  *
  * Boot-args:
  * - huskytouch=0: driver idle (default, opt-in).
- * - huskytouch=1: normal touch mode (reset, init, sense-on, event loop).
- * - huskytouch=2: probe mode (read-only: power domain, CMU, USI/SPI and GPIO registers).
+ * - huskytouch=1: touch: bring-up, active scan, event polling into HuskyHIDTouch.
+ * - huskytouch=2: bring-up probe: register dumps, USI enable, reset pulse,
+ *   CONTROLLER_READY wait, chip-ID read; no scanning.
  * - huskytouchdelay=N: initial delay in seconds (default 5).
  * - huskytouchpoll=N: polling interval in milliseconds (default 10).
- * - huskytouchinv=0/1: coordinate inversion for 1344x2992 panel (default 1).
+ * - huskytouchinv=0/1: invert both axes (default 0: the IC reports panel pixels,
+ *   0..1343 x 0..2991, DT st,max-coords).
  * - huskytouchdebug=1: verbose event logging.
  *
- * FTM5 Protocol:
- * - Hardware registers accessed via address-based commands:
- *   FTS_CMD_HW_REG_R = 0xB6, FTS_CMD_HW_REG_W = 0xB6.
- * - Chip ID read at address 0x0004 with 1 dummy byte -> 0x36 0x40.
- * - System reset at address 0x0028 with value 0x80.
- * - FIFO events read via 0x85 with 1 dummy byte (8 bytes per event packet).
- * - Event ID decoded from (ev[0] >> 4) & 0x0f.
- * - Touch ID from high nibble (ev[1] >> 4) & 0x0f; touch type from ev[1] & 0x0f.
- * - Remaining events count from ev[7] & 0x1f.
+ * FTM5 SPI protocol (google-modules touch/fts/ftm5, SPI build): hardware
+ * registers are read with 0xFB and written with 0xFA, each followed by a
+ * 4-byte big-endian address; every read returns one dummy byte first. The FIFO
+ * is read with 0x87 (8-byte events, byte 7 bits 4:0 = events still queued).
+ * Event IDs are whole bytes (0x03 controller ready, 0x13/0x23/0x33 touch
+ * enter/motion/leave). Reset = reset GPIO low 10 ms then high, after which the
+ * IC queues CONTROLLER_READY.
  *
  * Fail safe: if the hardware does not respond or the chip ID does not match,
- * the driver logs the result and cleanly gives up without hanging or panicking.
+ * the driver logs the result and gives up without hanging or panicking.
  */
